A Cloud Platform Governance Framework defines the rules, responsibilities, and operational standards for managing Azure environments consistently across an organization.

The framework generally addresses:

* Identity governance
* Resource organization
* Security policies
* Cost management
* Compliance requirements
* Monitoring standards
* Operational processes
* Documentation standards

For example, an enterprise operating across multiple countries can implement a unified governance framework to ensure every Azure subscription follows identical security and operational standards.

A real-life use case is multinational organizations maintaining consistent governance despite having independent business units.

A governance framework establishes operational consistency while reducing administrative complexity.
